joe Linux: build GNOME Settings without CUPS, gnome-bluetooth and ModemManager

gnome-control-center 51.1 requires all three unconditionally:

    cups_dep = dependency('cups', version : '>= 1.4', required: false)
    assert(cups_dep.found(), 'CUPS 1.4 or newer not found')
    mm_dep =  dependency('mm-glib', version: '>= 0.7')
    gnome_bluetooth_dep = dependency('gnome-bluetooth-ui-3.0')

and has no option to do without them. None of the three exists in joe
Linux, so this patch

  - drops the Printers, Bluetooth and Mobile Network (wwan) panels from the
    build (panels/meson.build, shell/cc-panel-loader.c) together with the
    dependency checks that only they need;
  - takes mobile broadband devices out of the Network panel, which is the
    only other user of libmm-glib: net-device-mobile.c is no longer built
    and cc-network-panel.c no longer talks to ModemManager. Wired, Wi-Fi,
    VPN and proxy settings are untouched;
  - leaves BUILD_WWAN and BUILD_BLUETOOTH undefined, which is what the
    remaining sources (the panel loader, the default applications page)
    already check.

